\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My God, how wonderful Thou art,
\par Thy majesty how bright!
\par How beautiful Thy mercy-seat,
\par In depths of burning light!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. How dread are Thine eternal years,
\par O everlasting Lord,
\par By prostate spirits day and night
\par Incessantly adored!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. How beautiful, how beautiful,
\par The sight of Thee must be,
\par Thine endless wisdom, boundless power,
\par And awful purity!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O how I fear Thee, living God,
\par With deepest, tenderest fears,
\par And worship Thee with trembling hope
\par And penitential tears!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Yet I may love Thee too, O Lord,
\par Almighty as Thou art,
\par For Thou hast stooped to ask of me
\par The love of my poor heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. No earthly father loves like Thee;
\par No mother, e'er so mild,
\par Bears and forbears as Thou hast done
\par With me, Thy sinful child.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Father of Jesus, love's reward,
\par What rapture will it be
\par Prostrate before Thy throne to lie,
\par And gaze, and gaze on Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

